      "release": {
        "tag": "v3.0.0-alpha.3",
        "published_at": "2026-10-30T04:28:31Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/AgoraIO/agora-agents-ts/releases/tag/v3.0.0-alpha.3",
        "notes": "- Support existing Customer ID/Secret HTTP Basic authentication alongside token007 for Platform and legacy requests. Optional App Certificates continue to sign RTC tokens without changing Basic REST authentication.\n\n- Generate Platform authorization with the official ConvoAI service, using agora-token 2.0.7 while preserving RTC and RTM expiration behavior.\n- Retain required provider language parameters for AssemblyAI, Google, Microsoft, Sarvam, and Speechmatics ASR. Default Sarvam TTS to bulbul:v3 without overriding explicit models."
      },
      "releases": [
        {
          "tag": "v3.0.0-alpha.3",
          "published_at": "2026-10-30T04:28:31Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/AgoraIO/agora-agents-ts/releases/tag/v3.0.0-alpha.3",
          "notes": "- Support existing Customer ID/Secret HTTP Basic authentication alongside token007 for Platform and legacy requests. Optional App Certificates continue to sign RTC tokens without changing Basic REST authentication.\n\n- Generate Platform authorization with the official ConvoAI service, using agora-token 2.0.7 while preserving RTC and RTM expiration behavior.\n- Retain required provider language parameters for AssemblyAI, Google, Microsoft, Sarvam, and Speechmatics ASR. Default Sarvam TTS to bulbul:v3 without overriding explicit models."
        },
        {
          "tag": "v3.0.0-alpha.2",
          "published_at": "2026-10-29T07:39:35Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/AgoraIO/agora-agents-ts/releases/tag/v3.0.0-alpha.2",
          "notes": "- Fix Platform provider defaults, Gemini/Bedrock credentials, ASR keywords/language/endpoints, and generic/HeyGen avatar mapping. Add typed MiniMax voice/audio controls.\n- Add explicit ephemeral and outbound-call session helpers, fixed-UID RTC token generation, full inbound call policy, optional extraction/secret metadata response types, and token-only client typing.\n- Make source builds portable and build Git installs through prepare. Keep compatibility CI tarball capture independent of prepare output. Correct saved-agent examples. Model availability for managed OpenAI is validated by the service.\n- Preserve Gemini credentials during endpoint normalization and capture RTC signing identity per session. Retain generated RTC tokens across failed-start retries, refresh them for new unkeyed session lifecycles, and leave unsupported UIDs to server provisioning. Reject mixed telephony and RTC options before normalization."
        },
        {
          "tag": "v3.0.0-alpha.1",
          "published_at": "2026-10-28T14:23:49Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/AgoraIO/agora-agents-ts/releases/tag/v3.0.0-alpha.1",
          "notes": "- Saved agents, ephemeral and saved-agent sessions, project secrets/numbers, and campaign resources are available in the preview checkout. See [Saving agents](docs/guides/saved-agents.md).\n- Aligned the preview with the bundled [OpenAPI contract](openapi.yaml): vendor-specific `credential.fields`, explicit secret references for saved credentials, optional session UID, session runtime PATCH, 50,000-contact/10 MiB campaigns, and current number/call-policy fields. Session and campaign create/action idempotency lasts 24 hours; writes do not retry automatically. Removed public campaign retry fields and advertised session analysis results.\n- The current preview service rollout is US-only. Regional availability may expand independently of SDK releases; this rollout note does not introduce a new SDK region restriction.\n\n- Saved-agent and ephemeral-session preview APIs support cascaded pipelines only. Removed realtime/MLLM from the preview contract and reject unsupported MLLM requests before HTTP. Existing inline MLLM sessions remain supported."
        }
      ]
    },
